$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure B for the stereoselective
cross-coupling of enolphosphates 1b and 4a-d with arylboronic acid.
Toluene (4mL/mmol) and 2 M aqueous potassium phosphate (1.4 mL/mmol or
1.8 mL/mmol) was added to a mixture of phosphate dibromide 1a,b,4a-d (1.0
eq.), boronic acid (1.4 eq . or 1.8 eq.), palladium acetate (0.02 eq., 2
mol %), triphenylphosphine (0.06 eq., 6 mol %). The resultant mixture was
stirred at 45 °C. Then the crude reaction mixture was diluted with ether,
washed with 1M KOH, water and brine. Organic layer was dried over MgSO4,
concentrated under reduce pressure and purification by column
chromatography afforded the pure product.
(Z)-(1-Bromo-1-phenylhexene-2-yl)(diethyl) phosphate (Z)- 3b. The title
compound was prepared according the general procedure B starting from 1b
(3.940 g, 10 mmol), phenylboronic acid (1.70 g, 14 mmol), palladium
acetate (0.045 g, 0.2 mmol, 2 mol %), triphenylphosphine (0.157 g, 0.6
mmol, 6 mol %), 2M aq. K3PO4 (14 mL), and toluene (40 mL). The reaction
mixture was stirred 8 h at 45 °C, following column chromatography (silica
gel, EtOAc-hexane 1:3, UV detection).
(Z)-(1-Bromo-1-(4-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)phenyl)buten-2-yl)(diethyl)
phosphate (Z)-5c. The title compound was prepared according the general
procedure starting B from phosphate 4b (1.830 g, 5 mmol),
4-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)phenylboronic acid (1.760 g, 7 mmol),
palladium acetate (0.022 g, 0.1 mmol, 2 mol %), triphenylphosphine (0.077
g, 0.3 mmol, 6 mol %), 2M aq. K3PO4 (7 mL), and toluene (20 mL). The
reaction mixture was stirred 8 h at 45 °C, following column
chromatography (silica gel, EtOAc-hexane 1:3, UV detection). 2.140 g
(87%) of the title compound as a yellowish oil. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3):
δ = 0.19 (s, 6H), 0.96 (s, 9H), 1.09 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 1.38 (dt, J =
7.6 Hz, J (P-H) = 1.0 Hz, 6H), 2.38 (dq, J = 7.2 Hz, J (P-H) = 1.1 Hz,
2H), 4.27 (dq, J = 7.3 Hz, J (P-H) = 7.2 Hz, 4H), 6.78 (d, J = 8.7 Hz,
2H), 7.18 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3): δ = -4.49,
11.89, 11.81, 16.07 (d, J (C-P) = 7.6 Hz), 25.08, 25.52, 64.68 (d, J
(C-P) = 6.0 Hz), 108.22 (d, J (C-P) = 9.9 Hz), 119.80, 130.54 overlapping
with 130.70, 148.95 (d, J (C-P) = 7.7 Hz), 155.89. HRMS (ESI): Calc. for
C20H34BrO5PSi+H+ [M+H+]: 493.1169; Found: 493.1171. Rf = 0.35.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
