$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-Dromo-4'-methyl-1,1'-biphenyl (7): A mixture of 5 (2.83 g, 10 mmol), 6
(1.63 g, 12 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (0.35 g, 0.3 mmol), and potassium carbonate
(2.76 g, 20 mmol) in 200 mL of toluene/ethanol/water (8/1/1 v/v/v) was
heated to reflux for 12 h under nitrogen. The reaction mixture was cooled
to room temperature, poured into water, and extracted twice with
dichloromethane. The combined organic layers were washed with saturated
brine solution and water, and dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate.
After filtration and solvent evaporation, the residue was purified by
silica-gel column chromatography using hexane/dichloromethane as eluent.
White solid, yield 82% (2.02 g). LC-MS (APCI): m/z 246.1 (C13H11Br, calcd
246.0044). The product was used for the next step without further
characterization.3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, Suzuki coupling
