$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Phenylnaphthalen-1-yl trifluoromethanesulfonate. To a toluene solution
(82 mL) of 2-bromonaphthalen-1-yl trifluoromethanesulfonate (2.94 g, 8.28
mmol) were added potassium phosphate (4.21 g, 19.8 mmol), phenylboronic
acid (1.20 g, 9.84 mmol), bis(triphenylphosphine) palladium dichloride
(0.420 g, 0.598 mmol), and lithium bromide (0.873 g, 10.1 mmol) at room
temperature. The mixture was refluxed for 22 h and then phosphate buffer
(pH 7) was added at room temperature. After the resulting mixture was
filtrated with suction, organic materials were extracted with ethyl
acetate three times. The combined extracts were washed with brine and
dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate. After removal of the solvent under
reduced pressure, the residue was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel (hexane/ethyl acetate 30:1). 2-phenylnaphthalen-1-yl
trifluoromethanesulfonate (2.20 g, ca 74%) as a yellow solid.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pinpoint-Fluorinated Phenacenes: New Synthesis and Solubility Enhancement
Strategies
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
